    "q-61965": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61965",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A soccer tournament began with $64$ teams. The number of teams reduced by $\\frac{1}{2}$ after every round. How many teams remained after $6$ rounds?",
      "worked_solution": "There were $64$ initially, and this number decreased by $\\frac{1}{2}$ every round. \n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ round, there were $64\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})$ teams remaining.\n\n- After $2$ rounds, there were $64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}$ teams remaining.\n\n- After $3$ rounds, there were $64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}$ teams  remaining.\n\n- $…$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that there were $64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{6}$ teams remaining after $6$ rounds.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
