    "q-103124": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103124",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A company initially had $40\\,320$ followers on a social media platform. If the number of followers declines by $\\frac{1}{8}$ every month after some bad publicity, which expression gives approximately the number of followers after $4$ months?",
      "worked_solution": "If the number of followers reduces by $\\frac{1}{8}$ every month, then $\\frac{7}{8}$ of the followers remains every month.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ month, there will be $40\\,320\\cdot (\\frac{7}{8})$ followers.\n\n- After $2$ months, there will be $40\\,320\\cdot {(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}$ followers.\n\n- After $3$ months, there will be approximately $40\\,320\\cdot {(\\frac{7}{8})}^{3}$ followers.\n\n- After $4$ months, there will be approximately $40\\,320\\cdot {(\\frac{7}{8})}^{4}$ followers.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
